Audit confirmed. Proceed to STEP 2 (BUILD). This replaces all earlier Step 2
and fallback instructions.

GOAL
Every status change on a Material Request or Purchase Request (all 35 statuses
in the audit) immediately sends an SMS to the CURRENT OWNER, the person who
must act next.

STRICT RULES
1. Do NOT change, rename, or delete any existing table, column, route, page, or
   lifecycle logic. Only add or extend notification code.
2. A failed SMS must NEVER block, roll back, or crash the procurement action.
3. If something existing must be touched, STOP and ask me first.
4. Use my audit table (status -> current owner) as the source of truth. If a
   status has an unclear owner, list it and ask me instead of guessing.

BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE
- Run `git show 075df0c` and tell me why SMS was disabled. Do not re-enable
  anything until I confirm the reason is solved.

NO OLD SMS
- Only NEW status changes made after go-live may send an SMS. Never send for
  old records, never backfill, and never fire from bulk imports, seeders, or
  data fixes. Clear any old pending SMS jobs first.

BUILD

A) Central status-to-owner map
- One config/service that gives, for each status, the owner role or the owner
  field (assigned_finance_staff_id, driver_employee_id, requested_by), plus
  optional FYI recipients such as the original requester.

B) One central hook for all transitions
- Send from one place after the database commit (DB::afterCommit), not copied
  into controllers. Move the existing SMS calls from notifyNextOwner,
  ProcurementHandoffNotificationService, and the controllers into this hook,
  and remove duplicates, so nobody gets two SMS for one change.
- Cover the gaps from the audit: delivered, closeThreeWayMatch,
  selectiveTransfer, splitAndProcess, sendToFinanceDirect, destroy (cancelled),
  reactivate, and all the MR controller triggers.

C) Recipient resolution (one central resolver for MR and PR)
- NORMAL CASE: the SMS goes ONLY to the current owner, in this order:
  direct person (driver, assigned finance staff, requester) -> project/store
  staff -> role holders. If a role has several users, send to all of them.
  The Global Admin does NOT receive these messages.
- FALLBACK CASE (only this one): if NO ONE is assigned to the owner role, send
  the SMS to the Global Admin instead, with the prefix:
  "[Role '{role}' Unassigned - Global Admin Action Required] {normal message}"
  Also treat a role as unassigned if none of its users has a valid phone
  number.
- Do not copy the Global Admin on messages that were delivered normally.
- If the Global Admin is also the normal owner, send one SMS only.
- Find the Global Admin by role, not by a hard-coded user ID.
- If the Global Admin also has no phone, log it as "undeliverable" and show it
  in the Failed SMS list.

D) Message format (one short SMS, clear action)
- "{PR/MR} #{number} ({site}): {what happened} by {name}. Action needed:
  {action}. Open: {link}"
- Emergency requests get the prefix [URGENT-EMERGENCY].
- Use Amharic and English if the ERP already has language settings.
- For FYI recipients (rejection, cancellation, completion), mark the message
  as FYI.

E) Send immediately
- Send once at the moment of the status change, with the existing 5-second
  timeout. Do not use a delayed queue.

F) Deduplication
- Keep the 60-second guard (record + status + recipient), but a legitimate
  repeat must still send (for example a receipt rejected, then re-uploaded and
  verified again). Include the status and a transition counter in the key.

G) Master switch and test mode
- Keep PROCUREMENT_SMS_ENABLED, but when OFF, log "skipped" in
  procurement_sms_logs instead of silently doing nothing.
- TEST MODE: when on, all SMS go only to one test phone number I set, with the
  real recipient's name in the message. The fallback is decided first, then
  the message is redirected.

H) Logging
- Log every attempt in procurement_sms_logs: record, status, intended role,
  actual recipient, message, result, error, and the fallback reason if any.
  Add a column or table only if essential.

I) Admin settings page (existing Procurement SMS Handoff Settings)
- Per status: owner role, message text, and an on/off switch.
- Failed SMS list (including undeliverable).
- Role coverage table: each role, the number of active users with a valid
  phone, and a red warning for any role with 0.

TESTS
- Every one of the 35 statuses sends exactly one SMS to the correct owner.
- Role has users: only they receive it, the Global Admin gets nothing.
- Role has no users: the Global Admin receives it with the warning prefix.
- Assigned driver or finance staff has no phone: falls back to the role, then
  the Global Admin.
- A gateway failure does not stop the status change.
- No duplicates, but a legitimate repeat still sends.
- No SMS for old records or bulk updates.
- Test mode redirects every message to the test phone.

DELIVERY
- List every file created or changed.
- Give me the final table: status -> owner -> message -> fallback behavior.